---
source: crates/wows-query/src/tools.rs
assertion_line: 342
expression: specs()
---
- name: find_ships
  description: "List ships by name, tier, class or nation, including ships in closed testing (status \"test\", counted in test). Returns name, GameParams index, tier, class, nation, group and status. With a name, a ship it names as the single-ship tools read it (exact name, alias such as \"DM\", initials or former name) comes first with name_match \"named\"; ships whose names merely contain it follow with name_match \"partial\"."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      name:
        type: string
        description: "Ship name or part of it, e.g. \"moines\". A name that names one ship exactly, by an alias such as \"DM\", by its initials or by a former name lists that ship first. Omit to list by the other filters."
      min_tier:
        type: integer
        description: "A ship tier, 1 to 11."
        minimum: 1
        maximum: 11
      max_tier:
        type: integer
        description: "A ship tier, 1 to 11."
        minimum: 1
        maximum: 11
      class:
        type: string
        enum:
          - destroyer
          - cruiser
          - battleship
          - aircraft_carrier
          - submarine
      nation:
        type: string
        description: "Nation as GameParams spells it, e.g. \"USA\", \"Germany\", \"Japan\", \"Russia\", \"United_Kingdom\"."
      include_event_variants:
        type: boolean
        description: "Include event, clan-battle and retired variants. Defaults to false."
      exclude_test_ships:
        type: boolean
        description: "Leave out ships in closed testing. Defaults to false: they are listed with status \"test\". A test copy of a released ship is listed only with event variants."
- name: ship_overview
  description: "Credit price and research XP of tech tree ships, the GameParams doubloon value (with a note when it is not how the ship is obtained, e.g. Armory ships sold for coal or steel), research tree predecessors and successors, group and upgrade slot count of one ship."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      ship:
        type: string
        description: "Ship name as the user wrote it, e.g. \"Des Moines\", or a GameParams index such as \"PASC020\"."
    required:
      - ship
- name: ship_armor
  description: "Armor of one ship: per hull zone the thinnest and thickest plate above the waterline, and every plate by collision material (Bow_*, St_* stern, Cit_* citadel, Cas_* casemate, SS_* superstructure) with thickness in mm."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      ship:
        type: string
        description: "Ship name as the user wrote it, e.g. \"Des Moines\", or a GameParams index such as \"PASC020\"."
    required:
      - ship
- name: ship_aircraft
  description: "Squadrons of a carrier, hybrid ship or ship with an air strike: role, aircraft, squadron size, attack flight size, payload per plane, ordnance kind (bomb, skip bomb, rocket, torpedo, depth charge), ammo type, damage per projectile and HE penetration, plus air strike charges, reload and range. With thickness_mm, says whether each ordnance defeats that plate."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      ship:
        type: string
        description: "Ship name, e.g. \"Midway\", \"Ise\" or \"Gouden Leeuw\"."
      thickness_mm:
        type: number
        description: "Plate thickness in mm to test each squadron's ordnance against."
    required:
      - ship
- name: ship_shells
  description: "Main and secondary battery shells of one ship: ammo type, caliber, HE/SAP penetration with and without Inertia Fuse for HE Shells, the thickest whole-mm plate AP overmatches, alpha damage, muzzle velocity and fire chance."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      ship:
        type: string
        description: "Ship name as the user wrote it, e.g. \"Des Moines\", or a GameParams index such as \"PASC020\"."
    required:
      - ship
- name: penetration_search
  description: "Find ships whose shells defeat a plate outright: HE or SAP penetration at least the thickness, or AP whose caliber overmatches it (caliber > 14.3 x thickness). Give thickness_mm, or target_ship with zone. Without ammo, returns separate HE, SAP and AP overmatch groups. Each group gives qualifying (ships that defeat the plate, listed in ships) and considered (ships under the same filters that fire that ammo), each as total and by_class. With a target ship and no tiers, searches the target's tier +-2."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      thickness_mm:
        type: number
        description: Plate thickness in mm to test against.
      target_ship:
        type: string
        description: "Ship whose armor is the target, e.g. \"Des Moines\"."
      zone:
        type: string
        description: "Zone or plate of the target ship: \"Bow\", \"Stern\", \"Cit\", \"Cas\", \"SS\", or a plate name from ship_armor. A zone uses its thinnest plate above the waterline."
      ammo:
        type: string
        enum:
          - AP
          - HE
          - SAP
        description: "Only this shell type. Omit to get separate HE penetration, SAP penetration and AP overmatch groups in one answer."
      ifhe:
        type: boolean
        description: Apply Inertia Fuse for HE Shells to HE penetration. Defaults to false.
      battery:
        type: string
        enum:
          - main
          - secondary
          - any
        description: Which guns to consider. Defaults to main.
      min_tier:
        type: integer
        description: "Lowest tier to include. With a target ship and no tier bounds, the target's tier +-2 is used."
        minimum: 1
        maximum: 11
      max_tier:
        type: integer
        description: "Highest tier to include. With a target ship and no tier bounds, the target's tier +-2 is used."
        minimum: 1
        maximum: 11
      class:
        type: string
        enum:
          - destroyer
          - cruiser
          - battleship
          - aircraft_carrier
          - submarine
      nation:
        type: string
        description: "Nation as GameParams spells it, e.g. \"USA\"."
      exclude_test_ships:
        type: boolean
        description: "Leave out ships in closed testing. Defaults to false: they are searched and counted under `test`. A test copy of a released ship is never searched."
- name: armor_trace
  description: "Trace a shooter's shell or bomb through a target ship's 3D armor model, e.g. whether Sekiryu's AP bombs can citadel Yamato or Des Moines AP can citadel a broadside cruiser at 10 km. Casts a grid of parallel rays along the line of fire (gun range and target angle, or the bomber's dive) and runs AP through every plate with the armor viewer's simulation; HE and SAP are tested against the first plate. Returns the fraction of rays over the citadel that detonate inside it, a summary per struck zone, example rays with their plates, a verdict, and the assumptions behind it."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      shooter:
        type: string
        description: "Firing ship, e.g. \"Des Moines\" or \"Sekiryu\"."
      target_ship:
        type: string
        description: "Target ship, e.g. \"Yamato\"."
      weapon:
        description: Defaults to main_battery.
        oneOf:
          - type: string
            enum:
              - main_battery
              - secondary_battery
          - type: string
            const: bombs
            description: "AP, HE or SAP bombs of the shooter's dive bombers or air strike."
      ammo:
        type: string
        enum:
          - AP
          - HE
          - SAP
        description: Shell or bomb type. Defaults to AP when the weapon has it.
      range_km:
        type: number
        description: "Gun range in km, 0 or more; 0 is point blank, flat at muzzle velocity. Required for guns, not used for bombs."
      target_angle_deg:
        type: number
        description: "Target heading away from broadside in degrees: 0 is broadside, 30 angled, 90 bow-on with the bow toward the shooter. For bombs, 0 is a dive across the ship and 90 a dive along it from bow to stern. Defaults to 0."
      target_hull:
        type: string
        description: "Target hull module, e.g. \"Hull B\". Defaults to the stock hull."
      ifhe:
        type: boolean
        description: Apply Inertia Fuse for HE Shells to gun HE penetration. Defaults to false.
      spacing_m:
        type: number
        description: "Distance between neighbouring rays in m, 0.25 to 10. Defaults to 1."
      aircraft:
        type: string
        description: "Aircraft name when the shooter carries several bomb-carrying squadrons, e.g. \"Ryusei\". Without it, squadrons with AP bombs come first, then stock dive bombers before researched or jet dive bombers, and those before the air strike."
    required:
      - shooter
      - target_ship
- name: citadel_profile
  description: "Shape and exposure of one ship's citadel from its 3D armor model: share of the citadel face above the waterline per side, roof height, slope of the citadel plates by height band (vertical, inclined belt, sloped deck, flat deck), whether it is a turtleback, and its height along the ship. For broadside flat fire, and for a shooter's main battery AP at range_km when given, the armor in front of the citadel (effective thickness spread and the least, median and most armored plate stacks with overmatch, ricochet and fuse events, over rays without a glancing strike, with the glancing rays counted apart) and how often the citadel plate is struck past 60 deg or past the ricochet angles."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      ship:
        type: string
        description: "Ship whose citadel is described, e.g. \"Yamato\"."
      hull:
        type: string
        description: "Hull module, e.g. \"Hull B\". Defaults to the stock hull."
      shooter:
        type: string
        description: "Ship whose main battery AP is fired at the citadel, e.g. \"Des Moines\". Needs range_km."
      range_km:
        type: number
        description: "Range in km for the shooter's plunging fire."
      spacing_m:
        type: number
        description: "Distance between neighbouring rays in m, 0.25 to 10. Defaults to 0.5."
    required:
      - ship
- name: ship_stats
  description: "Port stat card of one ship with stock modules. With captain skills and upgrades, lists the stats they change, from and to, and which skill or upgrade caused each change."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      ship:
        type: string
        description: "Ship name, e.g. \"Des Moines\"."
      skills:
        type: array
        items:
          type: string
        description: "Captain skills by name or acronym, e.g. [\"IFHE\", \"Concealment Expert\"]. Resolved in the ship's class tree."
      upgrades:
        type: array
        items:
          type: string
        description: "Upgrades by name, e.g. [\"Main Battery Modification 2\"]. One per slot."
      conditions_met:
        type: boolean
        description: "Treat conditional skill triggers as met, e.g. an enemy in secondary range for Close Quarters Combat. Defaults to false."
      hp_percent:
        type: number
        description: Remaining health in percent for health-scaled effects such as Adrenaline Rush. Defaults to full health.
      full_card:
        type: boolean
        description: "Include the full stat card. Defaults to true without skills or upgrades and false with them, when only the changes are listed."
    required:
      - ship
- name: ship_firing_arcs
  description: "Which guns and torpedo tubes of one ship bear on a target at each bearing: barrels bearing bow-on, stern-on (within 30 degrees) and on each broadside, where all barrels bear or never, damage of one salvo per ammo type, fires per minute and fire chance per salvo assuming every shell hits, and main battery dispersion at a range. Optional skills, upgrades and modules; guns or torpedoes that fit only another hull need that hull in modules too. Optional target_ship applies the target's fire resistance."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      ship:
        type: string
        description: "Ship name, e.g. \"Des Moines\"."
      modules:
        type: array
        items:
          type: string
        description: "Modules to mount instead of stock, e.g. [\"Hull B\"]. Omit for stock."
      skills:
        type: array
        items:
          type: string
        description: "Captain skills by name or acronym, e.g. [\"Demolition Expert\"]. They change reload and fire chance."
      upgrades:
        type: array
        items:
          type: string
        description: "Upgrades by name, e.g. [\"Main Battery Modification 3\"]. One per slot."
      target_ship:
        type: string
        description: "Ship being fired at, e.g. \"Colbert\". Its hull's fire-node probability scales the fire chance. Omit to use the shell's fire chance alone."
      range_km:
        type: number
        description: "Firing range in km for the dispersion ellipse, 0 or more; 0 gives the ellipse at the muzzle and ranges past the main battery's maximum use the maximum. Defaults to the maximum range."
    required:
      - ship
- name: stat_names
  description: "Every stat stat_search can compare, as \"name (unit, per item): label\". Includes armor zone plate thickness and total main battery barrels."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
- name: stat_search
  description: "Find ships whose stats meet every condition, e.g. [{\"stat\": \"artillery.reload_time\", \"op\": \"<\", \"value\": 5}]. Get stat names from stat_names. Lists ships that qualify stock, and ships that need modules, upgrades or captain skills, with the fewest needed. Returns counts of ships considered and qualifying, by class."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      conditions:
        type: array
        items:
          description: One condition on a stat.
          type: object
          properties:
            stat:
              description: "Stat name from stat_names, e.g. \"artillery.reload_time\" or \"armor.citadel.max\"."
              type: string
            op:
              description: "How a stat value compares to a condition's threshold."
              type: string
              enum:
                - "<"
                - "<="
                - ">"
                - ">="
                - "="
                - "!="
            value:
              description: Threshold in the unit stat_names lists for the stat.
              type: number
            qualifier:
              description: "Only the row with this qualifier: ammo type for shells (\"HE\", \"AP\", \"CS\"), torpedo, secondary mount or consumable name. Omit to accept any row."
              type: string
          additionalProperties: false
          required:
            - stat
            - op
            - value
        description: Conditions that must all hold.
      min_tier:
        type: integer
        description: "A ship tier, 1 to 11."
        minimum: 1
        maximum: 11
      max_tier:
        type: integer
        description: "A ship tier, 1 to 11."
        minimum: 1
        maximum: 11
      class:
        type: string
        enum:
          - destroyer
          - cruiser
          - battleship
          - aircraft_carrier
          - submarine
      nation:
        type: string
        description: "Nation as GameParams spells it, e.g. \"USA\"."
      include_event_variants:
        type: boolean
        description: "Include event, clan-battle and retired variants. Defaults to false."
      exclude_test_ships:
        type: boolean
        description: "Leave out ships in closed testing. Defaults to false: they are searched and counted under `test`. A test copy of a released ship is searched only with event variants."
    required:
      - conditions
- name: captain_skill
  description: "One captain skill by name, abbreviation (IFHE, SI, CE, SE, PT, IFA, AR, DE, BoS, RPF) or former name (BFT, AFT): description, point cost and effects per ship class, or for one ship's class with ship."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      skill:
        type: string
        description: "Skill name, e.g. \"Inertia Fuse for HE Shells\", a common abbreviation such as IFHE, SI, CE, SE, PT, IFA, AR, DE, BoS, or a former name such as BFT."
      class:
        type: string
        enum:
          - destroyer
          - cruiser
          - battleship
          - aircraft_carrier
          - submarine
        description: Only describe the skill for this class.
      ship:
        type: string
        description: "Only describe the skill for this ship's class, e.g. \"GK\". Overrides class."
    required:
      - skill
- name: skill_tree
  description: "The captain skill tree of one ship class, skill names by point cost."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      class:
        type: string
        enum:
          - destroyer
          - cruiser
          - battleship
          - aircraft_carrier
          - submarine
    required:
      - class
- name: upgrade
  description: "One upgrade (modernization) by name: slot, kind, credit price, effects per class and which tiers, nations and ships it fits."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      upgrade:
        type: string
        description: "Upgrade name, e.g. \"Main Battery Modification 2\" or \"Concealment System Modification 1\"."
      ship:
        type: string
        description: Ship to check the upgrade against; also selects the class for effects.
    required:
      - upgrade
- name: ship_upgrades
  description: "Every upgrade that fits one ship, by slot, with price and effects."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      ship:
        type: string
        description: "Ship name as the user wrote it, e.g. \"Des Moines\", or a GameParams index such as \"PASC020\"."
    required:
      - ship
- name: ship_consumables
  description: "Consumables of one ship by slot with charges, reload, action time, detection ranges and heal rate, optionally with captain skills and upgrades applied. consumable narrows to one, e.g. \"radar\", \"hydro\", \"DCP\"."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      ship:
        type: string
        description: "Ship name, e.g. \"Des Moines\"."
      consumable:
        type: string
        description: "Only this consumable, e.g. \"radar\", \"hydro\", \"Repair Party\", \"DCP\"."
      skills:
        type: array
        items:
          type: string
        description: "Captain skills by name or abbreviation, e.g. [\"SI\"], applied to the consumable stats."
      upgrades:
        type: array
        items:
          type: string
        description: "Upgrades by name, e.g. [\"Engine Boost Modification 1\"], applied to the consumable stats."
    required:
      - ship
- name: gameparams_query
  description: "Run a jq filter (jaq dialect) over raw GameParams entries, for values the other tools do not report. select is one entry {\"param\": \"PASC020\"} (name, index or id), one ship {\"ship\": \"Des Moines\"}, or a set {\"set\": {\"type\": \"Ship\", \"nation\": \"USA\", \"species\": \"Cruiser\", \"tier\": 10}} of at most limit entries. The filter runs once per entry with the entry object as input; entries without output are omitted. Entries are large: start with `keys`, then `.Field | keys`, then pick fields. Output is cut to max_bytes; when truncated, hint says how to narrow the filter. The filter has 5 seconds; env is not available."
  input_schema:
    type: object
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      select:
        oneOf:
          - type: object
            properties:
              param:
                type: string
            required:
              - param
            additionalProperties: false
            description: "One entry by param name (PASC020_Des_Moines_1948), index (PASC020)\nor numeric id."
          - type: object
            properties:
              ship:
                type: string
            required:
              - ship
            additionalProperties: false
            description: "One ship by English name, as the ship tools resolve it."
          - type: object
            properties:
              set:
                description: Entries matching every given field. Text matches without regard to case.
                type: object
                properties:
                  type:
                    description: "`typeinfo.type`, e.g. Ship, Projectile, Gun, Modernization, Ability,\nCrew, Unit, Exterior."
                    type: string
                  nation:
                    description: "`typeinfo.nation`, e.g. USA, Japan, Germany, Russia."
                    type: string
                  species:
                    description: "`typeinfo.species`, e.g. Cruiser, Destroyer, Artillery."
                    type: string
                  tier:
                    description: "The entry's `level` field: tier for ships and modules."
                    type: integer
                    maximum: 11
                    minimum: 1
                additionalProperties: false
                required:
                  - type
            required:
              - set
            additionalProperties: false
            description: "Entries of one `typeinfo.type`, in GameParams order."
        description: Which GameParams entries to read.
      filter:
        type: string
        description: "jq program (jaq dialect) run once per selected entry, with the entry\nobject as input. Start with `keys` to list fields, then narrow, e.g.\n`.A_Hull | keys` or `.A1_Artillery | {maxDist, sigmaCount}`."
      limit:
        type: integer
        maximum: 200
        minimum: 1
        description: "Most entries a set selection reads, 1 to 200, default 20."
      max_bytes:
        type: integer
        maximum: 24000
        minimum: 500
        description: "Output budget in bytes, 500 to 24000, default 6000."
    required:
      - select
      - filter
